AI Neural DB Project Guide
Bhai, tune jo file bheji hai, usme kuch jagah formatting toot gayi hai (jaise code blocks ``` gayab hain aur headings missing hain). Maine usko fix karke aur usme aur bhi zyada details, features, aur sections add kar diye hain.

Ye ekdam enterprise-grade (par practice ke hisaab se perfect) README ban gaya hai. Tu bas is poore code ko copy karke apne README.md file me paste kar de.

📄 Copy this complete updated README.md:
markdown
<div align="center">

# 🧠 Neural Vault

### AI Neural Database — Store & Search Any Data Type by Meaning, Not Keywords

[![FastAPI](https://img.shields.io/badge/Backend-FastAPI-009688?style=for-the-badge&logo=fastapi&logoColor=white)](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/)
[![React](https://img.shields.io/badge/Frontend-React-61DAFB?style=for-the-badge&logo=react&logoColor=black)](https://reactjs.org/)
[![PostgreSQL](https://img.shields.io/badge/Database-PostgreSQL-336791?style=for-the-badge&logo=postgresql&logoColor=white)](https://www.postgresql.org/)
[![Gemini](https://img.shields.io/badge/AI-Google%20Gemini-4285F4?style=for-the-badge&logo=google&logoColor=white)](https://deepmind.google/technologies/gemini/)
[![TailwindCSS](https://img.shields.io/badge/UI-TailwindCSS-38B2AC?style=for-the-badge&logo=tailwind-css&logoColor=white)](https://tailwindcss.com/)

**Powered by Gemini embeddings + pgvector. Unifies vectors, documents, code, images, audio, graphs & reasoning traces in one semantic engine. Build your AI's memory layer — no GPU required.**

</div>

---

## 📖 What is Neural Vault?

Traditional databases search by **exact match**. Neural Vault searches by **meaning**. 

Ask *"show me code about authentication"* and it finds relevant snippets — even if the word "authentication" never appears in the code. It acts as a single, unified memory layer for AI systems, storing and connecting multiple data modalities.

Whether you are building a RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) pipeline, a personal second brain, or a multi-modal code search engine, Neural Vault provides the semantic backbone to store and retrieve context intelligently.

## ✨ Key Features

- 🔢 **8 Data Types in One Engine**: Store Vectors, Documents, Code, Images, Audio, Knowledge Graphs, and AI Reasoning Traces seamlessly.
- 🔍 **Unified Semantic Search**: Query everything at once. Get results grouped by type based on semantic similarity.
- 🧠 **Gemini-Powered**: Auto-generates 768-dimension embeddings via Google Gemini API (`text-embedding-004`).
- 🖼️ **AI-Generated Metadata**: Automatically generates descriptions for images and transcripts for audio using `gemini-1.5-flash`.
- 🕸️ **Knowledge Graph**: Store nodes and relationships with semantic linking for complex data structures.
- 🧩 **Reasoning Traces**: Save step-by-step AI thinking processes for explainability and debugging.
- 💻 **CPU-Friendly**: Runs perfectly on any standard laptop. No GPU required — all heavy lifting is done by the Gemini API.
- 🎨 **Premium UI**: Beautiful, AI-native dashboard built with React + TailwindCSS (Dark mode by default).
- 🔐 **Clean Architecture**: Backend built with FastAPI, SQLAlchemy (ORM), and Alembic for safe database migrations.
- ⚡ **Fast & Async**: Fully asynchronous API endpoints for high performance.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| **Backend** | Python 3.10+, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, Alembic, Uvicorn |
| **Frontend** | React 18, Vite, TailwindCSS, Framer Motion, Axios |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL 15+ with `pgvector` extension |
| **AI / Embeddings** | Google Gemini API (`text-embedding-004`, `gemini-1.5-flash`) |

## 🏗️ System Architecture

```text
       [ React Frontend (Vite + Tailwind) ]
                      ⬇
               (REST API / Axios)
                      ⬇
       [ FastAPI Backend (Python) ]
                      ⬇
        (SQLAlchemy ORM & Services)
                      ⬇
       [ PostgreSQL + pgvector DB ]
                      ⬆
       (Vector Similarity Search)
                      ⬆
       [ Google Gemini Embeddings ]
📂 Project Structure
text
neural-vault/
├── backend/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── models/       # SQLAlchemy DB Models
│   │   ├── schemas/      # Pydantic Data Validation
│   │   ├── routers/      # API Endpoints
│   │   ├── services/     # Business Logic & Gemini API calls
│   │   └── main.py       # FastAPI Entry Point
│   ├── alembic/          # Database Migrations
│   └── requirements.txt
├── frontend/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/   # Reusable UI Components
│   │   ├── pages/        # 8 Dashboard Pages
│   │   ├── api/          # Axios API calls
│   │   └── App.jsx
│   └── package.json
├── database/
│   └── schema.sql        # Raw SQL for DB setup
└── README.md
🚀 Getting Started
Follow these steps to set up the project locally on your machine.

Prerequisites
Python 3.10+ installed

Node.js 18+ installed

PostgreSQL 15+ installed (with pgvector extension)

Google Gemini API Key (Get it from Google AI Studio)

1. Database Setup
bash
# Create the database
psql -U postgres -c "CREATE DATABASE neural_vault;"

# Connect to the database and enable pgvector
psql -U postgres -d neural_vault -c "CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;"
2. Backend Setup
bash
# Navigate to backend folder
cd backend

# Create and activate virtual environment
python -m venv venv
# Windows: venv\Scripts\activate 
# Mac/Linux: source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Create a .env file and add your credentials
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/neural_vault

# Run database migrations
alembic upgrade head

# Start the FastAPI server
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
API Docs will be available at http://localhost:8000/docs

3. Frontend Setup
bash
# Open a new terminal, navigate to frontend folder
cd frontend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start the development server
npm run dev
The React app will be available at http://localhost:5173

🔌 API Endpoints (Overview)
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/vectors	Store a raw vector embedding
POST	/api/documents	Upload & auto-chunk a document
POST	/api/code	Store source code snippets with language metadata
POST	/api/images	Upload image & auto-generate description
POST	/api/audio	Upload audio & auto-generate transcript
POST	/api/graph	Create nodes and edges for knowledge graph
POST	/api/reasoning	Save AI reasoning traces
GET	/api/search	Unified semantic search across all data types
💡 Use Cases
AI Memory System: Give your AI a long-term, multi-modal memory.

RAG Knowledge Base: Retrieval-Augmented Generation for apps.

Code Search Engine: Find code by meaning, not just keywords.

Personal Second Brain: Store everything and search intelligently.

📸 Screenshots
(Yahan apne project ke Dashboard aur Search page ke screenshots add karna jab UI ready ho jaye)

🤝 Contributing
This is a practice project, but contributions, issues, and feature requests are welcome! Feel free to check the issues page.

📝 License
Distributed under the MIT License. See LICENSE for more information.

<div align="center"> <i>Built with ❤️ as a practice project focusing on clean architecture and semantic AI integration.</i> </div> ```
🚀 Isko GitHub Par Kaise Daalein?
Terminal me ye commands run kar:

bash
git add README.md
git commit -m "docs: upgraded README with complete project details, architecture, and setup guide"
git push -u origin main
Ab jaake apna GitHub repo refresh kar, ekdam premium aur professional dikhega! Interviewer ko first impression hi solid milega. 🚀

giginore files
Bhai, GitHub par code push karte time .gitignore file bahut zaroori hoti hai. Ye file batati hai ki kaunsi files aur folders ko GitHub par upload NAHI karna hai.

Agar tu ye file nahi banayega, toh tera venv folder, node_modules, teri API keys (.env file), aur temporary files sab GitHub par chali jayengi — jo bahut bura lagta hai aur security risk bhi hai.

Maine tere project ke hisaab se ek perfect .gitignore file banayi hai jisme Backend (Python), Frontend (React/Node), Database, aur VS Code ki saari faltu files ignore ho jayengi.

📄 Step 1: .gitignore File Banao
Apne project ke root folder (jahan se tune git init kiya tha) me ek nayi file banao jiska naam .gitignore ho (dhyaan rahe, starting me dot . hai).

Notepad open kar aur ye poora code copy-paste kar de:

gitignore
# ==========================================
# 1. ENVIRONMENT & SECRETS (Sabse Important)
# ==========================================
# API keys aur passwords kabhi push nahi karne chahiye
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.production
*.pem
*.key

# ==========================================
# 2. PYTHON / BACKEND (FastAPI)
# ==========================================
# Virtual Environment folders
venv/
env/
.venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# Python compiled files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Testing & Coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Database files
*.db
*.sqlite3

# ==========================================
# 3. NODE / REACT FRONTEND
# ==========================================
# Dependencies (Ye bahut heavy hota hai, push mat karna)
node_modules/

# Production build files
/build/
/dist/
.vite/

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ==========================================
# 4. UPLOADS & DATA (Practice Project Rules)
# ==========================================
# User dwara upload ki gayi images/audio/docs
backend/uploads/images/*
backend/uploads/audio/*
backend/uploads/documents/*
backend/uploads/code/*

# Par folders empty na dikhein isliye .gitkeep rakhte hain
!backend/uploads/images/.gitkeep
!backend/uploads/audio/.gitkeep
!backend/uploads/documents/.gitkeep
!backend/uploads/code/.gitkeep

# ==========================================
# 5. VS CODE / OS FILES
# ==========================================
# Editor settings
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
📄 Step 2: .env.example File Banao (Extra Pro Tip)
Interviewer ko ye bahut achha lagta hai ki tune apni secrets ko protect kiya hai. Ek aur file bana jiska naam .env.example ho. Isme actual API key mat daalna, bas format dikhana hai.

env
# Backend Environment Variables Example
# Is file ko copy karke '.env' banao aur apni real keys daalo

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/neural_vault
PORT=8000
🚀 Step 3: GitHub Par Push Karo
Ab terminal me ye commands run kar:

bash
# 1. Saari nayi files add karo
git add .

# 2. Commit karo
git commit -m "chore: added .gitignore and .env.example for security"

# 3. GitHub par push karo
git push -u origin main
Bhai, ab tera repo ekdam clean aur secure ho gaya hai. node_modules aur venv jaise 10,000 files GitHub par upload hone se bach gaye hain. Ab tu aaram se coding shuru kar sakta hai! 🚀




